  "title": "Kourovka problem 19.13 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "The well-known Baer–Suzuki theorem states that if every two conjugates of\nan element a of a finite group G generate a finite p-subgroup, then a is contained in\na normal p-subgroup. Does such a theorem hold in the class of periodic groups for\np > 2?\n   A counterexample is known for p = 2; see Archive 11.11a).            A. V. Borovik",
    "sha256": "a6a9155051ff3364c2a9dc13fbd05c7f4c4e0ad96c49614de2cfcd940503914b",
